nd and the little animations that make ticking things off feel good.`,skills:`Product Design, Figma, Motion`,link:``,image:void 0},{kind:`project`,title:`Orbit UI Kit`,folder:`Work`,page:1,desc:`A design system of 120 components with tokens, docs and a playground. Adopted by three teams in the first month.`,skills:`Design Systems, React, Storybook`,link:``,image:void 0},{kind:`project`,title:`Lumen Brand`,folder:`Work/Branding`,page:1,desc:`Identity for an indie lighting studio: logo, packaging and a pixel-art launch site.`,skills:`Branding, Illustration, Framer`,link:``,image:void 0},{kind:`project`,title:`Nochy Eat`,folder:`Work/Branding`,page:1,desc:`Aplikasi layanan pesan-antar makanan berbasis Flutter dengan sistem multi-role, realtime tracking, dan payment gateway.`,skills:`Flutter, Dart, Supabase, Midtrans`,link:``,image:`/framerusercontent-com/sites/icons/BG-SORE.jpg`},{kind:`app`,app:`resume`,title:`Resume`,folder:``,page:1,desc:``,skills:``,link:``,image:void 0},{kind:`note`,title:`Read me`,folder:``,page:1,desc:`Welcome to my desktop!

- Open the Work folder for projects
- Contact has my links
- Certificates holds my credentials
- Social Media has my links
- Drag windows around, resize them from the corner
- Try the Piano`,skills:``,link:``,image:void 0},{kind:`link`,title:`My CV`,folder:``,page:1,desc:`ZAIDAN_CV_PRO.PDF`,skills:``,link:`/ZAIDAN_CV_PRO.PDF`,image:void 0},{kind:`note`,title:`Sketchbook`,folder:``,page:2,desc:`This item lives on desktop page 2.
Set a different Page number on any file to move it.`,skills:``,link:``,image:void 0}],iconStyle:`color`,name:`Zaidan Ahmad Ath Thoriq`,role:`Software Enginer, Product Manager, Quality Assurance`,bio:`The Journey of a Boy Slowly Learning About the World\n\nHello, my name is Zaidan. You can call me Jay, Zaidan, or whatever you prefer. This time, I want to tell you a little about myself.\n\nI was born in Banjarnegara, Indonesia, on November 19, 2005.\n\nChildhood — Kindergarten\nI think I first became aware of the world around me when I was about five or six years old. Back then, I was still in kindergarten. There is one thing I remember quite clearly: I was often the last child waiting to be picked up.\n\nI used to arrive at school early and go home late. Not because I was particularly hardworking or loved spending time at school, but because both of my parents had to be at school by six in the morning. Oh, by the way, both of my parents are teachers. They were always busy with their responsibilities, but I knew they were doing everything they could to secure a better future for my younger sibling and me.\n\nMy family did not come from a wealthy background. In fact, our financial situation was quite difficult back then. Still, I never felt that I lacked love and care.\n\nElementary School — When the World Still Seemed Kind\nAfter kindergarten, I continued my education at an Islamic elementary school. I still remember my first day in Grade 1. My father dropped me off at the classroom door and told me I would be going home with the school transport driver.\n\nGrade 1 was also when I discovered one of my biggest fears: needles. That fear never really went away. Even now, needles are still among the things I fear the most.\n\nGrade 2 — Feeling Like the Main Character\nI was placed in Grade 2 Pantas, a special class for students who performed well academically. At that moment, I felt like I had finally proven that I was capable of something special.\n\nThis was also when I started noticing economic differences among my classmates. Some of them travelled to other cities during holidays, while mine were usually limited to visiting my grandmother. For the first time, I began to understand that people did not grow up with the same privileges.\n\nGrade 5 — The First Time I Realized the World Wasn't That Kind\nEntering Grade 5 was when things started to change. I was punched, pinched, and bullied. My books were scribbled on, and my school uniform was sometimes covered in unwanted marks.\n\nStrangely enough, I never told my parents about any of it. Maybe I did not want to look weak. I just tried to get through each day.\n\nEventually, I decided to study harder. I wanted to improve my grades and return to a class with my old friends. And finally, when I entered Grade 6, I managed to do just that.\n\nVocational High School — Memories, Lessons, and Growing Up\nAfter junior high school, I continued my education at a vocational high school, majoring in Computer and Network Engineering.\n\nGrade 11 — Six Months That Taught Me a Lot\nI had the opportunity to complete an internship in Purwokerto. I helped repair ODP cables, inspected ODC equipment, and visited a Telkom server room. One of the people I remember most was a technician named Mas Adit — genuinely kind, friendly, and easygoing.\n\nWhen the internship finally ended, I felt something I had not expected. It was difficult to say goodbye to people I had not even known before those six months began.\n\nThat experience taught me something: every meeting eventually comes with the possibility of saying goodbye.\n\nMy First Major Failure\nI failed to get accepted into university through both the SNBP and SNBT entrance examinations. Honestly, I was devastated. I had spent three years studying computers, only to be expected to master three years of general high school subjects in just one month.\n\nEventually, with my family\u2019s support, I continued my education at Universitas Ahmad Dahlan. And that was where the next chapter of my life began.\n\nSemester Seven — When Dreams Meet Reality\nNow, I am in my seventh semester. I used to dream of working at major companies like Gojek, Shopee, or Google. But the closer I get to the working world, the more reality starts to challenge those dreams.\n\nI have applied to several internship programs, but the results were always the same: rejection. I know my skills might not be good enough yet. But sometimes, I cannot help wondering: after all the projects I have built, is there really not a single company willing to give me a chance?\n\nNow, I am starting to consider a different path. I want to take my English skills more seriously and explore opportunities to work abroad.\n\nThe Ending — A Story That Has Not Finished Yet\nIf I had to summarize my life so far, I think there is one thing that has changed more than anything else: the way I see the world.\n\nThere are two song lyrics I always remember whenever life gets difficult.\n\n\u201cWhen your beautiful dreams never come true, well, just let it be.\u201d\n\u201cIf I made it through yesterday, then I can face tomorrow too.\u201d\n\nI am Zaidan. Some people know me as Jay. And this is my story. Not the story of someone who always gets what he wants, but the story of someone who keeps moving forward.\n\nTo be continued...`,avatar:`/aku%20jay.jpg`,facts:``,email:`jydnahm@gmail.com`,socials:[{label:`GitHub`,url:`https://github.com`},{label:`LinkedIn`,url:`https://www.linkedin.com`},{label:`Instagram`,url:`https://www.instagram.com`}],osName:`FolioOS`,music:void 0,musicOnEnter:!1,intro:!0,introTitle:``,sections:!0,wall:`#c9c3bd`,floor:`#cfd6e4`,wood:`#a8683c`,accent:`#5aa0ff`,bg:`#f3ece3`,mood:`sunset`,weather:`clear`,pet:`cat`,pet2:`none`,petName:``,pet2Name:``,paintingImage:void 0,easelImage:void 0,paintingTitle:`Dusk at sea`,paintingNote:`A favourite piece. Swap it for your own work in the property panel.`,readingList:ol,references:jl,faqs:Ml,chatIntro:``,resumeUrl:``,resumeText:Nl,trinkets:Pl,goodreadsUrl:``,pixelFont:`pixelify`,customFont:``,playlist:[{title:`The Art of Chasing You`,url:`https://youtu.be/z8J8fOHdpPw?si=dyQLejKAC33Yw47O`},{title:`1 2 3`,url:`https://youtu.be/prte4HRo2ew?si=F0nkmG9ab2qP2CPU`},{title:`bunga`,url:`https://youtu.be/5XXl46ZcXSA?si=80JrhXIg62FBF3YM`}],petHue:0,petAccessory:`none`,pet2Hue:0,pet2Accessory:`none`,frameStyle:`gold`,frameColor:`#e0b050`,petScale:1,petFollow:!0,hints:!0,chips:!1,ambient:!0,sound:!1,builtIn:!0,moodButton:!0,petButton:!0,lightButton:!0,musicButton:!0,caption:`Click the computer, shelves, lamp and curtains.`,status:`Open to work`},Zl=Ls,Ql=[`None`,`Cat`,`Dog`,`Bunny`,`Chick`,`Slime`],le(ks,{status:{type:D.String,title:`Status`,defaultValue:`Open to work`,description:`Shown in the OS menu bar. Leave empty to hide.`},files:{type:D.Array,title:`Files & folders`,description:`Everything on the OS desktop. Use Folder like Work or Work/Branding to nest, and Page to put items on other desktop pages. Pick App shortcut to place Resume, Chatbox, Mail or any other built-in app as an icon.`,control:{type:D.Object,controls:{kind:{type:D.Enum,title:`Type`,options:[`project`,`link`,`note`,`image`,`app`],optionTitles:[`Project`,`Link`,`Note`,`Image`,`App shortcut`],defaultValue:`project`},app:{type:D.Enum,title:`Opens`,options:cc.map(e=>e[0]),optionTitles:cc.map(e=>e[1]),defaultValue:`resume`,hidden:e=>e.kind!==`app`},title:{type:D.String,title:`Name`,defaultValue:`Untitled`},folder:{type:D.String,title:`Folder`,defaultValue:``,placeholder:`Empty = desktop. Work/Branding`},page:{type:D.Number,title:`Desktop page`,min:1,max:6,step:1,displayStepper:!0,defaultValue:1},desc:{type:D.String,title:`Text`,displayTextArea:!0,defaultValue:`What it is and what you did.`,hidden:e=>e.kind===`app`},skills:{type:D.String,title:`Skills`,description:`Comma separated`,defaultValue:``,hidden:e=>e.kind!==`project`},link:{type:D.Link,title:`Link`,hidden:e=>e.kind===`note`||e.kind===`app`},image:{type:D.Responsive